+ * often omits the path, and `error.message` sometimes carries the only
+ * operational fact there is -- a shell timeout summary, a spawn failure --
+ * while `llmContent` holds unrelated output. So both are sent: the
+ * model-facing half first, then the operational summary when it is not
+ * already part of it. A tool that writes the same text into both, which is
+ * the common case, is unaffected byte for byte.
